      "description": "•\tPrincipal architect and hands-on technical manager for the Enterprise Java Application Framework which is the foundation of flagship product Web of Knowledge, today’s premier research platform for information in the sciences, social sciences, arts, and humanities; \n•\tExecuted and delivered day-to-day technical solutions; daily operation: planning, prioritization and resource allocation; responsible for WOK’s core business functionalities, quality, performance and security; As a key contributor, helped transform Web of Knowledge from silo'ed applications into a feature rich world-class scholarly scientific research platform w/ updated architecture and technologies. \n•\tBuilt the team from ground-up;  built talents and grew team members; nurtured,mentored, educated and trained diverse teams of developers; Managed both onshore and offshore teams.\n•\tExperienced with budgeting and resources planning/forecasting/scoping/allocation;\n•\tGather requirements; perform business and system analysis; translate functional requirements into solutions; \n•\tReviewed architecture and code regularly; led implementation and solved the hardest problems; led research, evaluation and innovation; instituted best practices and maintained the culture of configuration based architecture, unit test, code review, continuous integration and internal training and knowledge sharing;\n•\tReduced code/design complexity; improved performance, consistency and reusability; reduced costs; shortened typical development/release cycle;",
